“I am an IAM user, but I want to temporarily become this role and use its permissions.”

🧠 Real-Life Example (Best way to understand)
Office example 🏢
You are an employee (IAM User)

Your company has a server room (AWS resources)

The server room key is NOT given permanently

When needed, you borrow a temporary access card (IAM Role)

That temporary card:

Works for limited time

Has limited permissions

Automatically expires

📌 That borrowing = Assume Role

❌ Old / Bad Way (Not Production)
IAM User
 └── AdministratorAccess (permanent power 😱)
Problems:

Permanent credentials

Full access

Huge security risk

✅ Correct Production Way
IAM User (no power)
   |
   | AssumeRole (STS)
   v
IAM Role (temporary power)
🧩 Key AWS Components (Beginner Friendly)
Term	Meaning
IAM User	A person (you)
IAM Role	A set of permissions
