This error is very common when using Terraform S3 backend with DynamoDB locking 👍
Good news: nothing is broken — one required resource is missing.

I’ll explain from very basics, then give exact steps to fix.

❌ The REAL Problem (Simple Words)
Terraform is saying:

❝ I want to use DynamoDB table terraform-lock for state locking,
but this table DOES NOT EXIST ❞

That’s it. ✅

🔍 Understanding the Error Message
Key line:
ResourceNotFoundException: Requested resource not found
DynamoDB table "terraform-lock"
Terraform backend config:

dynamodb_table = "terraform-lock"
➡️ Terraform does NOT create this table automatically
➡️ You must create it yourself

🧠 What is Terraform State Locking? (Beginner)
When multiple people / pipelines run Terraform:

Terraform uses DynamoDB to lock the state

Prevents two applies at the same time

Avoids state corruption

Terraform ---> DynamoDB (lock)
           ---> S3 (state file)
✅ SOLUTION (PRODUCTION CORRECT WAY)
STEP 1️⃣ Create DynamoDB Lock Table (REQUIRED)
You can do this manually once (recommended for beginners).

Option A: Create via AWS Console (EASIEST)
Go to AWS Console

Open DynamoDB

Click Create table

Table details:
Field	Value
Table name	terraform-lock
Partition key	LockID
Type	String
Billing	On-demand (PAY_PER_REQUEST)
👉 No sort key
👉 No indexes

Click Create table

Option B: Create via AWS CLI
aws dynamodb create-table \
  --table-name terraform-lock \
  --attribute-definitions AttributeName=LockID,AttributeType=S \
  --key-schema AttributeName=LockID,KeyType=HASH \
  --billing-mode PAY_PER_REQUEST \
  --region ap-south-1
STEP 2️⃣ Verify Table Exists
aws dynamodb list-tables
You should see:

terraform-lock
STEP 3️⃣ Required IAM Permissions
Your Terraform role/user MUST have:

{
  "Effect": "Allow",
  "Action": [
    "dynamodb:GetItem",
    "dynamodb:PutItem",
    "dynamodb:DeleteItem",
    "dynamodb:DescribeTable"
  ],
  "Resource": "arn:aws:dynamodb:ap-south-1:<ACCOUNT_ID>:table/terraform-lock"
}
⚠️ If this is missing → same error again

STEP 4️⃣ Re-run Terraform
terraform init -reconfigure
terraform plan
✅ Lock will be acquired successfully

⚠️ IMPORTANT NOTE ABOUT WARNING YOU SAW
You earlier saw:

The parameter "dynamodb_table" is deprecated
Meaning:
Terraform is slowly moving to S3 native locking

DynamoDB locking is still supported

You can safely ignore for now

